{
"content_id": "23044",
"reference_id": 22212,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Obadiah 1:2–4",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "31001002-31001004",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p><span><em>I will make you small</em></span>: Several messages of judgment describe Edom’s specific sins against Israel (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"31001010\" data-end-ref=\"31001014\">Obadiah 1:10–14</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"24049007\" data-end-ref=\"24049022\">Jeremiah 49:7–22</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26025012\" data-end-ref=\"26025014\">Ezekiel 25:12–14</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26036005\" data-end-ref=\"26036005\">36:5</data>). Edom often appears among the nations that opposed Israel and the Lord (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"23034001\" data-end-ref=\"23034017\">Isaiah 34</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26035001\" data-end-ref=\"26036038\">Ezekiel 35–36</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"30009001\" data-end-ref=\"30009015\">Amos 9:1–15</data>). </p></li><li><p><em>small among the nations … The pride of your heart</em>: Edom’s rocky landscape reflected the pride of its people. Just as their land was high and difficult to reach, the people of Edom thought they were secure and above others. The height of the mountain fortress that provided their security only highlights the height from which Edom would fall. Edomite princes were among the arrogant rulers of the nations (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26032029\" data-end-ref=\"26032029\">Ezekiel 32:29</data>; compare <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"01036001\" data-end-ref=\"01036043\">Genesis 36</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"13001043\" data-end-ref=\"13001054\">1&nbsp;Chronicles 1:43–54</data>).</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "31001002",
"start_ref_usfm": "OBA 1:2",
"end_ref": "31001004",
"end_ref_usfm": "OBA 1:4"
