{
"content_id": "23033",
"reference_id": 22201,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Obadiah 1:10–14",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "31001010-31001014",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p><span><em>Because of the violence against your brother Jacob</em></span>: The reason for Esau’s condemnation is explained in <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"31001010\" data-end-ref=\"31001010\">Obadiah 1:10</data> (see also <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"23034001\" data-end-ref=\"23034017\">Isaiah 34</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"24049007\" data-end-ref=\"24049022\">Jeremiah 49:7–22</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"29003019\" data-end-ref=\"29003019\">Joel 3:19</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"30001011\" data-end-ref=\"30001012\">Amos 1:11–12</data>) and expanded in <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"31001011\" data-end-ref=\"31001014\">Obadiah 1:11–14</data>, where Edom’s betrayal is described. In legal terms, these verses provide evidence for the charge of breaking a covenant.</p>",
