{
"content_id": "23035",
"reference_id": 22203,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Obadiah 1:12–14",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "31001012-31001014",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>All societies are responsible for wrongdoings, like those of Edom (see, for example, the messages against Israel’s neighbors in <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"30001003\" data-end-ref=\"30002003\">Amos 1:3–2:3</data>). The Edomites committed sins against Judah by helping the Babylonians loot the land (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"31001013\" data-end-ref=\"31001013\">Obadiah 1:13</data>) and either killing or sending back Judah’s escapees (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"31001014\" data-end-ref=\"31001014\">1:14</data>).</p>",
