{
"content_id": "23037",
"reference_id": 22205,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Obadiah 1:15–18",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "31001015-31001018",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>The law of retribution (<em>lex talionis</em>) means we face the consequences of our actions. Edom&apos;s betrayal and pride would lead to her own downfall when vengeance came. Justice would deliver Israel and punish Edom (see also <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"24049007\" data-end-ref=\"24049022\">Jeremiah 49:7–22</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"26032029\" data-end-ref=\"26032029\">Ezekiel 32:29</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"39001002\" data-end-ref=\"39001005\">Malachi 1:2–5</data>).</p>",
