"content_id": "23039",
"reference_id": 22207,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Obadiah 1:17",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "31001017",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Jerusalem would become a safe place for those who escape. A small group from Judah stayed in Jerusalem (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"24040011\" data-end-ref=\"24040012\">Jeremiah 40:11–12</data>). The Lord’s mountain of refuge stands in stark contrast to Edom’s failed cliff fortresses. </p></li><li><p><em>their possession</em>: The land God gave to Abraham (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"01012001\" data-end-ref=\"01012007\">Genesis 12:1–7</data>) would be returned to his descendants forever. </p></li><li><p><em>the house of Jacob</em>: The prophet Malachi mentioned the promise of return for the people of Judah, but not for the Edomites (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"39001004\" data-end-ref=\"39001005\">Malachi 1:4–5</data>).</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
